## Public interface and dependency rules

Web consumers use packages/core/index.ts as the public core interface. Storage access stays inside core; the public index may export storage-backed operations. For example, packages/web/public.ts imports price from ../core/index.ts and quote() returns 12. Checkout obtains servicePrice through the same interface. No web consumer may import or re-export another core file, including through a path alias; no exceptions are accepted.

